# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Orbit — Android / Gradle / Kotlin
#  Rule of thumb: if Gradle or Android Studio can regenerate it,
#  or if it only makes sense on this one machine, it stays out.
#
#  NOTE: comments must be on their own line. Git does not support
#  trailing comments — "foo.txt  # why" is treated as a pattern
#  containing spaces and a hash, and silently matches nothing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ---- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
# ~80 MB of generated code, classes and APKs. Regenerated by ./gradlew build.
build/
app/build/
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

# ---- Gradle ----------------------------------------------------------------
# local.properties holds YOUR Android SDK path — it is machine specific.
.gradle/
local.properties
gradle-app.setting

# ---- Kotlin ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Session directory created by the Kotlin 2.x compiler daemon.
.kotlin/

# ---- IDE -------------------------------------------------------------------
# .idea holds local paths (gradleJvm, SDK locations) and per-machine window
# state. Nothing in it is needed to build the project.
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/

# ---- Signing & secrets -----------------------------------------------------
# Never commit these. A leaked keystore cannot be revoked — anyone holding it
# can publish updates that Android will accept as genuinely yours.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
signing.properties
secrets.properties
*.p12
*.pem

# ---- Build artifacts -------------------------------------------------------
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.aar
*.dex
*.class
output.json
release/

# ---- Logs & lint reports ---------------------------------------------------
*.log
hs_err_pid*
.navigation/
lint-results*.html
lint-results*.xml

# ---- OS noise --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Temporary files -------------------------------------------------------
# The last pattern is Word's lock file, created while a .docx is open.
*~
*.swp
*.tmp
*.bak
~$*.docx
